    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d347">

                <pb facs="0382" n="292" sameAs="frus:frus1918Russiav02/pg292"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 861.00/2275</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of State to the Ambassador in
                        Japan</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Morris</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1918-07-17T18:00:00-04:00"><hi rendition="#italic">July 17, 1918,
                                6 p.m.</hi></date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Your July 15, 5 p.m., last two sentences. The American Government has
                    communicated through the Japanese Ambassador here a proposal to Japan that the
                    United States and Japan each send a small contingent of 7,000 men to assist the
                    Czecho-Slovak troops in Siberia, this to be followed by an economic mission.</p>
                <p>The British and French Ambassadors were informed. The Japanese will have the high
                    command. No reply as yet from Japan. The plans for an economic mission are
                    temporarily held in abeyance pending result of above.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Polk</hi></signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
